    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Hurricane was settled in 1896 as part of Brigham Young's Cotton Mission to establish southern Utah for agricultural purposes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hurricane%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early residents of Hurricane Valley relied on a canal that took eleven years to construct between 1893 and 1904.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://utahguide.com/cities/hurricane/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Hurricane is historically known for its small farms and orchards producing peaches, pecans, and pistachio nuts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
